      "text": "To find the probability that it will rain on both days, we can multiply the probabilities of rain on Saturday and Sunday together since the events are independent (\"no leaping\" and \"no overnight sleaptits\").\n\nThe probability of rain on Saturday is given as 60%, or 0.6. The probability of rain on Sunday is given as 25%, or 0.25.\n\nMultiplying these two probabilities together, we get:\n\n\\[ \\text{Probability of rain on both Saturday and Sunday} = 0.6 * 0.25 = 0.15 \\]\n\nTo express this as a percent, we multiply by 100:\n\n\\[ 0.15 \\times 100 = 15\\% \\]\n\nSo, the probability that it will rain both on Saturday and Sunday is $\\boxed{15\\%}$.",
